  "facts": [
    "The Mount Baker Tunnel, completed in 1940, was the world’s largest soft‑earth tunnel, 63 feet in diameter, bored through clay to carry eight freeway lanes and a dedicated bicycle‑pedestrian path.",
    "In 1989 a brand‑new 63‑foot tunnel opened north of the originals, adding a double‑deck roadway with three general‑purpose lanes, two reversible HOV lanes, and a separate light‑rail track.",
    "The 1993 expansion doubled the tunnel’s length, covering the old west portal with a 2,000‑foot concrete lid and converting the original tubes to eastbound‑only traffic, while the new tunnel handled westbound traffic."
